Wine port
=========

Base: WINE_SHA in pins.env. scripts/02-fetch.sh applies the patches here in
order, each as a commit on the pin (apply_series in scripts/common.sh), so
third_party/wine's history is the port: git log there lists these patches,
git diff shows only what is not recorded yet, and git checkout of a file
restores the port's version. Each file is its commit's message, a line "---",
and the diff.

To change the port, edit third_party/wine and run scripts/save-patches.sh. It
folds each edit into the patch that changes that file (for a new file, the one
patch that changes its directory) and writes the series out again. When no
single patch owns a file, it says which commit to make by hand. A new commit
in third_party/wine becomes a new patch in its place and wants a line here.

Each file belongs to one patch. 0005, 0006 and 0008 only link together on iOS.

0001  build against the iOS SDK: configure, SDK shims, the container path's case
0002  interfaces shared with the app and FEX: the relocated shared data, the
      gamepad snapshot, the arena write alias query
0003  wineserver as a thread of the app; the full administrator token; the
      running-program count
0004  the server's desktop window stands in for explorer's
0005  per-process state behind accessors on ntdll's unix side
0006  Windows child processes as threads: process context, private ntdll,
      fd cache, reaper
0007  win32u's classes, GDI bindings and display keys per process
0008  memory (virtual.c): the JIT arena, PE images through its write alias,
      the ARM64EC map, bigpool, stack pool, swap file, CEF soft pools,
      mid-size bands, Win32 error codes, child exit reclaim, diagnostics
0009  the TEB in x28; stores replayed through the arena's write alias; fault
      reports
0010  KUSER_SHARED_DATA at its iOS address on the Win32 side
0011  CPU features, gamepads and thread QoS from the host
0012  starting from a prebuilt prefix
0013  Steam workarounds in process creation: lean mode, web helper flags
0014  FreeType linked statically
0015  wineios.drv, the display driver
0016  Steam's UI without explorer: hover menus, the tray
0017  audio through RemoteIO
0018  controllers from the app: XInput, device notifications
0019  nsi and nsiproxy without routing sockets
0020  trust roots from the app's CA bundle

The unix side is built with -ffixed-x28 -DWINE_TEB_IN_X28 -DWINE_IOS_JIT_ARENA
(scripts/11-wine-ios.sh).
